# REST client examples. Set credentials locally; never commit real secrets.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@eventId = 1
@guideId = 1
@userId = 123
@adminUsername = replace-locally
@adminPassword = replace-locally
@csrfToken = paste-token-from-csrf-response

### Public catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events?eventType=TREKKING&page=0&size=20

### Public event
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}

### Public guides
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/guides?specialization=trek

### Keep the returned session cookie and copy data.token for subsequent writes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tour/csrf
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}

### Create draft; copy response data.eventId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/events
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventName": "Ta Nang trekking",
  "eventType": "TREKKING",
  "description": "Two days trekking and camping",
  "location": "Lam Dong",
  "basePrice": 1500000,
  "details": {
    "durationMinutes": 2880,
    "difficultyLevel": "MODERATE",
    "meetingPoint": "TerraPeak Outpost",
    "requirements": "Trekking shoes and raincoat"
  }
}

### Upload before publishing; replace local image path
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/events/{{eventId}}/images
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=TourImageBoundary

--TourImageBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Trail photo
--TourImageBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="trail.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./trail.jpg
--TourImageBoundary--

### Publish
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/events/{{eventId}}/status
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"PUBLISHED"}

### Create guide from an existing active account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/guides
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId":{{userId}},"experienceYears":3,"specialization":"Mountain trekking"}

### Public guide
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/guides/{{guideId}}
